Now I understand! The commit ebc366b introduced the `imageFormat()` function that selects the QImage format based on the TGA header:

```cpp
static QImage::Format imageFormat(const TgaHeader &head)
{
    ...
    } else if (info.grey) {
        format = QImage::Format_Grayscale8;  // 8-bit!
    } else if (info.pal) {
        format = QImage::Format_Indexed8;    // 8-bit!
    } else {
        format = QImage::Format_RGB32;
    }
    ...
}
```

So for greyscale images, the QImage is `Format_Grayscale8` (1 byte per pixel). For paletted images, the QImage is `Format_Indexed8` (1 byte per pixel).

But the conversion loop for greyscale images writes `QRgb` (4 bytes) per pixel:
```cpp
} else if (info.grey) {
    auto scanline = reinterpret_cast<QRgb*>(img.scanLine(y));
    for (int x = 0; x < tga.width; x++) {
        if (tga.pixel_size == 16) {
            scanline[x] = qRgba(*src, *src, *src, *(src + 1));
            src += 2;
        } else {
            scanline[x] = qRgb(*src, *src, *src);
            src++;
        }
    }
}
```

Wait, but the fix commit f933cbe was made AFTER ebc366b. So the code in the repo (which is the vulnerable version) should have the `imageFormat()` function. Let me check:
